{
  "text": "2011B13 Outline the physiological role of cerebrospinal fluid, including\na description of its production and fate.\nList:\n·\nCSF\ncycle\n·\nCSF functions\n·\nCSF vs\nplasma\nCSF cycle:\nLocation\n·\n150mL total\n·\n50% in the ventricles\n·\n50% in the subarachnoid space of cerebral\n  cortex and spinal cord\nProduction\n·\nBy choroid plexus of first, second, third\n  ventricles and ependymal cells\n·\n500mL/day, constant production if\n  cerebral perfusion pressure >70mmHg\n·\nComplete turnover every 24 hours\nCirculation\n·\nDue to pulsatile flow in choroidal\n  arteries\n·\nLateral -> third -> fourth\n·\nFourth -> around cerebral hemispheres\n  via foramen of Magendi and foramina of Luschka\n·\nFourth -> down central canal of spinal\n  cord\nReabsorption\n·\n90% into arachnoid villi superior\n  sagittal sinus\n·\n10% Into spinal arachnoid villi ->\n  epidural venous sinuses\n·\nMinimal below ICP 7mmHg. Linear increase\n  from ICP 7-23mmHg.\nGraph\nNote: X axis unit mmCSF not\n  mmHg\nNote: Y axis zero point not\n  at the X axis\n(Ganong’s Review of Medical\n  Physiology)\nCSF functions:\nPhysical protection\n·\nCushion surrounding the brain\n·\nLow specific gravity due to low protein\n  content (1.005 cf. 1.03 Plasma)\n·\nReduces effective weight of brain from\n  1.4kg -> 40g\n·\nHence ↓inertia, ↓risk of injury if sudden\n  change of direction\nICP buffer\n·\n↑ICP -> spinal displacement of CSF\nElectrolyte homeostasis\n·\nBBB and B-CSF-B are impermeable to most\n  ions\n·\nActive transport maintains\n  concentrations.\n·\nStable ionic environment essential for\n  brain electrical activity\nAcid-base homeostasis\n·\nBBB and B-CSF-B are impermeable to H\n+\nand OH\n-\n·\nStable pH important for brain activity\n  e.g. during intense exercise with lactic acidosis\nControl of breathing\n·\nCO\n2\ncan cross BBB, H+ cannot\n·\nCO\n2\nplasma -> CSF ->\n  brain ECF\n·\nCO\n2\n+ H\n2\nO <->\n  H\n+\n+ HCO\n3\n-\nNutrient and waste transport\n·\nActive transport between blood <->\n  CSF <-> brain ECF\nComparison to plasma:\nPlasma\nCSF\nAppearance\nYellowish\nClear, colourless\nSG\nWhole blood 1.06\nPlasma 1.03\n1.005\nOsmolality\n289\n289\nNa\n+\n140\n140\nK\n+\n4\n2.4\nCl\n-\n100\n114\nHCO\n3\n-\n24\n24\nMg\n2+\n1\nHigher\nCa\n2+\n2.4\n1.2 (50%)\nGlucose\n5\n3 (60%)\nProtein\n70g/L\n0.2g/L\npH\n7.4\n7.32\npCO\n2\n40\n50\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
